window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e25dfff3918fe597"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"sign-in-with-chatgpt-through-a-gateway\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt\">通过网关使用 ChatGPT 登录</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可取得该页的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"why-you-would-want-this\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">为什么要这样做</h2> <p>如果您已经有模型网关，并通过 API Platform 使用 Codex，可以在切换到<strong>通过 ChatGPT 登录</strong>时继续保留这个网关。这样既能保留模型网关，又能使用符合条件的 ChatGPT 工作区功能和控制选项（例如<a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597?anchor=voice-through-a-gateway\"><strong>语音模式</strong></a>）。不同登录方式的比较见<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7?anchor=feature-availability\">功能可用性</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-set-it-up\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">如何设置</h2> <p>现有的<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">命令辅助认证</a>会将网关密钥放在 <code>Authorization</code> 中。通过 ChatGPT 登录时，这个请求头承载的是 ChatGPT 令牌。因此，需要另外选择一种方式提供网关凭据：</p> <ul> <li><strong>方案 A：</strong> 用一个小型启动辅助程序复用现有的凭据命令，通过单独的请求头发送同一个网关密钥。</li> <li><strong>方案 B：</strong> 让 Codex 通过原生 OAuth 获取网关凭据。</li> </ul> <p>将选定的提供商配置加入工作区在云端管理的 <code>requirements.toml</code>；参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。这些要求在用户通过 ChatGPT 登录后生效，不会限制其他登录方式。网关与 Codex 兼容的基础 URL 必须将 <code>/models</code> 和 <code>/responses</code> 代理到 <code>https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"option-a-reuse-your-credential-command-with-a-helper\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"a\">方案 A：用辅助程序复用凭据命令</h3> <p>保留现有的凭据命令。一个小型辅助程序在启动 Codex 之前运行该命令，并将其输出导出为 <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code>。这仍是您现在使用的同一个网关密钥；变化的只是传递它的请求头。</p> <p>例如，现有的 API／提供商配置可能如下：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># config.toml — existing API/provider setup\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-gateway-token\"\n</code></pre> <p>对于 ChatGPT 登录，将该提供商配置替换为下面的托管配置。删除原有的 <code>auth</code> 配置块：命令辅助的提供商认证不能与 <code>requires_openai_auth = true</code> 同时使用。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># requirements.toml\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/backend-api/codex\" # Keep the gateway route.\nrequires_openai_auth = true # Use the ChatGPT credential for OpenAI.\nenv_http_headers = { \"X-Gateway-Key\" = \"GATEWAY_KEY\" } # Send the same gateway key separately.\n</code></pre> <p>在 CLI 中，可以使用下面这样的 shell 函数作为启动辅助程序。将其中的命令及参数替换为现有 <code>auth</code> 配置块中的命令及参数：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-sh\">codex_with_gateway() (\n  set -eu\n  GATEWAY_KEY=$(/usr/local/bin/fetch-gateway-token)\n  test -n \"$GATEWAY_KEY\"\n  export GATEWAY_KEY\n  exec codex \"$@\"\n)\n\ncodex_with_gateway\n</code></pre> <p>配置网关，使其接受并验证 <code>X-Gateway-Key</code>，然后在将请求转发给后端前删除这个请求头。此时，从客户端发出的请求携带以下信息：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-http\">Authorization: Bearer &lt;ChatGPT token&gt;\nChatGPT-Account-ID: &lt;workspace ID, when available&gt;\nX-Gateway-Key: &lt;same gateway key returned by your command&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>辅助程序每次启动只运行一次。Codex 不会重新运行它，也不会刷新这个请求头；密钥过期后，需要获取新密钥并重新启动。对于桌面应用，您的启动集成必须将 <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code> 提供给应用进程。如果希望由 Codex 管理网关登录及令牌续期，请选择方案 B。</p> <p>图中简写了请求头和启动辅助程序。请使用 <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;ChatGPT token&gt;</code>，并保留上面示例中辅助程序对空密钥的检查。如果 <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code> 为空，Codex 会省略 <code>X-Gateway-Key</code>。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">方案 A：通过启动辅助程序复用凭据命令。同一个网关密钥从 Authorization 移到 X-Gateway-Key，而 ChatGPT 登录提供 Authorization。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-header-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>方案 A：通过启动辅助程序复用凭据命令。同一个网关密钥从 Authorization 移到 X-Gateway-Key，而 ChatGPT 登录提供 Authorization。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-header-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">方案 A 的运行流程：网关验证并删除 X-Gateway-Key，然后将 ChatGPT Authorization 和任何账号 ID 原样转发至 Codex 后端。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-header-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>方案 A 的运行流程：网关验证并删除 X-Gateway-Key，然后将 ChatGPT Authorization 和任何账号 ID 原样转发至 Codex 后端。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-header-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"option-b-use-native-gateway-oauth\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"b-oauth\">方案 B：使用原生网关 OAuth</h3> <p>选择此方案，可以用 Codex 管理的网关登录替代凭据命令和启动辅助程序。网关必须有 OAuth 授权服务器。注册一个支持授权码和 PKCE 的公共客户端，然后替换示例中的 URL 和客户端 ID。删除现有提供商的 <code>auth</code> 配置块，并使用以下托管配置。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># requirements.toml\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/backend-api/codex\" # Keep the gateway route.\nrequires_openai_auth = true # Use the ChatGPT credential for OpenAI.\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.gateway_oauth] # Add gateway OAuth.\nauthorization_url = \"https://login.example.com/oauth/authorize\"\ntoken_url = \"https://login.example.com/oauth/token\"\nclient_id = \"YOUR_PUBLIC_CLIENT_ID\"\ndelivery = { kind = \"cookie\", name = \"auth-openid\" } # Add gateway auth as a cookie.\n# redirect_port = 43127\n</code></pre> <p>默认情况下，Codex 使用一个空闲的本机回环端口。如果身份提供商要求固定的重定向 URI，请设置 <code>redirect_port</code>，并为本示例注册 <code>http://127.0.0.1:43127/callback</code>。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">方案 B：用原生网关 OAuth 替代基于 API 密钥的网关认证，同时保留 ChatGPT 登录。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>方案 B：用原生网关 OAuth 替代基于 API 密钥的网关认证，同时保留 ChatGPT 登录。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">方案 B 的运行流程：网关验证并移除自己的 OAuth Cookie，然后将 ChatGPT 凭据转发至 Codex 后端。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>方案 B 的运行流程：网关验证并移除自己的 OAuth Cookie，然后将 ChatGPT 凭据转发至 Codex 后端。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"add-routing-headers-optional\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">添加路由请求头（可选）</h3> <p>无论使用哪个方案，Codex 都可以向网关发送自定义路由请求头。例如，在云端管理的 <code>requirements.toml</code> 中，为同一个 <code>enterprise_gateway</code> 提供商添加以下请求头：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.http_headers]\nx-portkey-config = \"&lt;gateway-routing-config-id&gt;\"\nx-portkey-metadata = '{\"tool_id\":\"codex\"}'\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会在模型提供商请求中发送这些请求头，网关负责应用路由规则。对于从 Codex 进程环境中读取的值，使用 <code>env_http_headers</code>。测试一次请求，确认网关收到了这两个请求头，并选择了预期的路由。更多请求头选项见<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">自定义模型提供商</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-credentials-on-their-own-paths\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">各类凭据分别处理</h3> <p>Codex 会发送 ChatGPT 的 <code>Authorization</code> 请求头、存在时的 <code>ChatGPT-Account-ID</code> 请求头，以及网关请求头或 Cookie。让网关验证并删除自己的凭据，然后原样转发 ChatGPT 请求头。</p> <p><a id=\"caveats-and-limitations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">注意事项与限制</h2> <ul> <li>使用支持托管模型提供商要求的 Codex 构建版本；方案 B 还要求支持原生网关 OAuth。旧构建版本可能忽略或拒绝不支持的字段。</li> <li>此路由涵盖通过所选模型提供商发出的请求。ChatGPT 登录、MCP、插件及其他应用连接可能使用不同的路径。</li> <li>网关可以看到请求数据和两种凭据。请在日志中隐去这些敏感信息；绝不要将网关凭据转发到上游。</li> <li>原生网关 OAuth 需要浏览器和可访问的本机回环回调，不提供设备码后备方式。如果没有刷新令牌，访问令牌过期时，用户必须重新通过浏览器登录。</li> <li>通用的 OpenAI <code>/v1/models</code> 响应不足以满足要求：Codex 需要一个 <code>models</code> 数组。请测试模型列表、一次提示词请求，以及部署中实际使用的每项功能。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"voice-through-a-gateway\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">通过网关使用语音</h3> <p>这套设置为 Codex 的模型提供商请求配置路由，不会启用 <a href=\"#/article/a-3b6d55bd01328040\">ChatGPT Voice</a>。对于 WebRTC 语音会话，通话创建和侧带连接使用不同的路由。<code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中的实验性设置 <code>experimental_realtime_webrtc_call_base_url</code> 只改变创建通话时使用的 HTTP 基础 URL，不会重定向侧带连接、媒体或普通模型请求。使用此覆盖设置之前，请与 OpenAI 一起核实通话目的地及凭据处理方式，然后测试一个完整的语音会话。</p> <p>有关 API／提供商凭据路径，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>。有关这些托管设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"sign-in-with-chatgpt-through-a-gateway\">Sign in with ChatGPT through a gateway</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"why-you-would-want-this\">Why you would want this</h2> <p>If you already have a model gateway and use Codex with the API Platform, you can keep your gateway while moving to <strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong>. This gives you access to eligible ChatGPT workspace features and controls (e.g. <a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597?anchor=voice-through-a-gateway\"><strong>voice mode</strong></a>) while keeping your model gateway. Compare the sign-in methods in <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7?anchor=feature-availability\">Feature availability</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-set-it-up\">How to set it up</h2> <p>Existing <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">command-backed authentication</a> places the gateway key in <code>Authorization</code>. With ChatGPT sign-in, that header carries the ChatGPT token. Choose how to supply the separate gateway credential:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Option A:</strong> Reuse your credential command through a small launch helper. Send the same gateway key in a separate header.</li> <li><strong>Option B:</strong> Let Codex obtain the gateway credential through native OAuth.</li> </ul> <p>Add the selected provider configuration to your workspace's cloud-managed <code>requirements.toml</code> in <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a>. These requirements apply after users sign in with ChatGPT; they do not restrict other sign-in methods. The gateway's Codex-compatible base URL must proxy <code>/models</code> and <code>/responses</code> to <code>https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"option-a-reuse-your-credential-command-with-a-helper\">Option A: Reuse your credential command with a helper</h3> <p>Keep your existing credential command. A small helper runs it before launching Codex and exports its output as <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code>. This is the same gateway key you use today; only its delivery header changes.</p> <p>For example, your existing API/provider configuration might contain:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># config.toml — existing API/provider setup\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-gateway-token\"\n</code></pre> <p>For ChatGPT sign-in, replace that provider with the following managed configuration. Remove its <code>auth</code> block: command-backed provider auth cannot be combined with <code>requires_openai_auth = true</code>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># requirements.toml\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/backend-api/codex\" # Keep the gateway route.\nrequires_openai_auth = true # Use the ChatGPT credential for OpenAI.\nenv_http_headers = { \"X-Gateway-Key\" = \"GATEWAY_KEY\" } # Send the same gateway key separately.\n</code></pre> <p>Use a launch helper such as this shell function for the CLI. Replace the command and arguments with those from your existing <code>auth</code> block:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-sh\">codex_with_gateway() (\n  set -eu\n  GATEWAY_KEY=$(/usr/local/bin/fetch-gateway-token)\n  test -n \"$GATEWAY_KEY\"\n  export GATEWAY_KEY\n  exec codex \"$@\"\n)\n\ncodex_with_gateway\n</code></pre> <p>Configure your gateway to accept <code>X-Gateway-Key</code>, validate the key, and remove that header before forwarding the request to the backend. The request from the client now carries:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-http\">Authorization: Bearer &lt;ChatGPT token&gt;\nChatGPT-Account-ID: &lt;workspace ID, when available&gt;\nX-Gateway-Key: &lt;same gateway key returned by your command&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>The helper runs once per launch. Codex does not rerun it or refresh this header; when the key expires, obtain a new key and relaunch. For desktop, your launch integration must supply <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code> to the app process. Choose Option B if you want Codex to manage gateway sign-in and token renewal.</p> <p>The diagrams abbreviate the request headers and launch helper. Use <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;ChatGPT token&gt;</code> and keep the helper's empty-key check from the examples above. If <code>GATEWAY_KEY</code> is empty, Codex omits <code>X-Gateway-Key</code>.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Option A: Reuse the credential command through a launch helper. The same gateway key moves from Authorization to X-Gateway-Key while ChatGPT sign-in supplies Authorization. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-header-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Option A: Reuse the credential command through a launch helper. The same gateway key moves from Authorization to X-Gateway-Key while ChatGPT sign-in supplies Authorization. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-header-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Option A runtime: The gateway validates and removes X-Gateway-Key, then forwards ChatGPT Authorization and any account ID unchanged to the Codex backend. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-header-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Option A runtime: The gateway validates and removes X-Gateway-Key, then forwards ChatGPT Authorization and any account ID unchanged to the Codex backend. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-header-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"option-b-use-native-gateway-oauth\">Option B: Use native gateway OAuth</h3> <p>Use this option to replace the command and launch helper with Codex-managed gateway sign-in. Your gateway must have an OAuth authorization server. Register a public client that supports authorization code with PKCE, then replace the example URLs and client ID. Remove the existing provider's <code>auth</code> block and use the following managed configuration.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># requirements.toml\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise_gateway\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway]\nname = \"Enterprise gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/backend-api/codex\" # Keep the gateway route.\nrequires_openai_auth = true # Use the ChatGPT credential for OpenAI.\n\n[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.gateway_oauth] # Add gateway OAuth.\nauthorization_url = \"https://login.example.com/oauth/authorize\"\ntoken_url = \"https://login.example.com/oauth/token\"\nclient_id = \"YOUR_PUBLIC_CLIENT_ID\"\ndelivery = { kind = \"cookie\", name = \"auth-openid\" } # Add gateway auth as a cookie.\n# redirect_port = 43127\n</code></pre> <p>Codex uses a free loopback port by default. If your identity provider requires a fixed redirect URI, set <code>redirect_port</code> and register <code>http://127.0.0.1:43127/callback</code> for this example.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Option B: Replace API-key gateway auth with native gateway OAuth alongside ChatGPT sign-in. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Option B: Replace API-key gateway auth with native gateway OAuth alongside ChatGPT sign-in. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-before-after-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Option B runtime: The gateway consumes its OAuth cookie and forwards the ChatGPT credential to the Codex backend. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-light.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Option B runtime: The gateway consumes its OAuth cookie and forwards the ChatGPT credential to the Codex backend. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/gateways/chatgpt-gateway-runtime-light.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"add-routing-headers-optional\">Add routing headers (optional)</h3> <p>With either option, Codex can send custom routing headers to the gateway. For example, add these headers to the same <code>enterprise_gateway</code> provider in your cloud-managed <code>requirements.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise_gateway.http_headers]\nx-portkey-config = \"&lt;gateway-routing-config-id&gt;\"\nx-portkey-metadata = '{\"tool_id\":\"codex\"}'\n</code></pre> <p>Codex sends the headers on model-provider requests; the gateway applies the routing rules. Use <code>env_http_headers</code> for values read from the Codex process environment. Test a request to confirm the gateway receives both headers and selects the intended route. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">Custom model providers</a> for more header options.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-the-credentials-on-their-own-paths\">Keep the credentials on their own paths</h3> <p>Codex sends the ChatGPT <code>Authorization</code> header, any <code>ChatGPT-Account-ID</code> header, and the gateway header or cookie. Have the gateway verify and remove its credential, then forward the ChatGPT headers unchanged.</p> <h2 id=\"caveats-and-limitations\">Caveats and limitations</h2> <ul> <li>Use a Codex build that supports managed model-provider requirements and, for Option B, native gateway OAuth. Older builds may ignore or reject unsupported fields.</li> <li>This route covers requests through the selected model provider. ChatGPT sign-in, MCP, plugins, and other app connections can use different paths.</li> <li>Your gateway can see request data and both credentials. Redact them in logs; never forward gateway credentials upstream.</li> <li>Native gateway OAuth needs a browser and a reachable loopback callback. It has no device-code fallback. Without a refresh token, users must repeat browser sign-in when the access token expires.</li> <li>A generic OpenAI <code>/v1/models</code> response is insufficient: Codex expects a <code>models</code> array. Test the model list, a prompt, and each feature your deployment uses.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"voice-through-a-gateway\">Voice through a gateway</h3> <p>This setup routes Codex model-provider requests; it does not enable <a href=\"#/article/a-3b6d55bd01328040\">ChatGPT Voice</a>. For WebRTC voice sessions, call creation and the sideband connection use separate routes. The experimental <code>experimental_realtime_webrtc_call_base_url</code> setting in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> changes only the HTTP base URL for call creation. It does not redirect the sideband connection, media, or ordinary model requests. Work with OpenAI to verify the call destination and credential handling before using this override, then test a complete voice session.</p> <p>For the API/provider credential path, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a>. For these managed settings, see <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration Reference</a>.</p>"};
